  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.96,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U3", "FB2"],
      "pins": ["U3.12", "FB2.1", "FB2.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "/V_{pH}"],
      "observed": "The pH isolator U3 pin 12, named V_ISO, is connected to the main GND net. The pH isolated supply node /V_{pH} is also connected to GND through ferrite bead FB2 (pin 1 on /V_{pH}, pin 2 on GND).",
      "expected": "U3 pin 12 should be on the pH isolated power output net and connected through FB2 to /V_{pH}, as U4 pin 12 is connected to /VISO_{EC} and then through FB4 to /V_{EC}. The pH isolated +5V domain should not be tied to primary GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"12\") (pinfunction \"V_{ISO}\") (pintype \"power_out\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"70\") (name \"/V_{pH}\") ... (node (ref \"FB2\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"FB2\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Each isolated EZO channel (U3 for pH, U4 for EC) derives its own isolated +5V (/V_pH, /V_EC) and isolated ground (/GNDISO_pH, /GNDISO_EC) internally from the ADM3260's isoPower feature"}
      ],
      "impact": "The pH-side isolated supply output is shorted/loaded to primary ground. This can disable or damage the U3 ADM3260 isoPower supply, remove power from the EZO-pH circuit, and defeat the intended galvanic isolation of the pH channel.",
      "confidence": 0.96
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist contains a clear connectivity anomaly on the pH isolated I2C bridge: U3 pin 12 (V_ISO) and the pH isolated supply node are tied to GND, unlike the EC channel and the stated design intent. This would likely make the pH EZO channel unpowered/nonfunctional and compromise its isolation."
}

